@page
@model MarketLens.Pages.DataModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Data sources"; }
<div class="workspace">
    <div class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">NO BROKERAGE LOGIN</p><h1>Market data, directly.</h1><p class="muted">@(Model.UsesMarketstack ? "Daily US research with an owner-managed API connection." : "Search listed companies and retrieve public data without provider sign-in.")</p></div></div>
    @if (Model.Notice is not null) { <aside class="notice">@Model.Notice</aside> }
    <div class="dashboard">
        @if (Model.UsesMarketstack) {
        <section class="panel setup-panel"><h2>Marketstack daily data</h2><p class="status">Personal US starter version · No brokerage login</p>
            <p>Search the 10-stock starter catalogue: Apple, Microsoft, NVIDIA, Amazon, Alphabet, Meta, Tesla, JPMorgan, Visa and Walmart. Search uses no API requests. Each uncached price fetch uses one request for up to one year of daily history.</p>
            <p>The free provider plan lists 100 requests per month. Prices are cached for 24 hours; Render sleep/restarts clear the cache, so returning later may consume another request. API quota is shared by your website, not granted separately to every visitor.</p>
            <p>Setup: create a free Marketstack account and set <code>MarketData__MarketstackApiKey</code> in Render Environment. Set <code>Hosting__OwnerPassword</code> to a private password of at least 12 characters. Website username: <code>owner</code>. Do not put either secret in GitHub. Save and redeploy.</p>
            <p>Daily charts and weeks/months analysis are supported when complete adjusted prices are available. No live quotes, intraday signals or fundamental long-term analysis. Malaysia and other markets are not enabled in this connector.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://marketstack.com/pricing">Provider plan details →</a>
        </section>
        } else {
        <section class="panel setup-panel"><h2>Public market data</h2><p class="status">No user login · No brokerage account · No API key</p>
            <p>Research now uses public Yahoo Finance responses. Search by company name or symbol, then fetch that listing's daily prices and available annual financial data.</p>
            <p>Examples: <strong>Maybank → MY.1155</strong>, <strong>Apple → US.AAPL</strong>, <strong>Tencent → HK.00700</strong>. The adapter recognises 26 market prefixes, including Malaysia, US, Hong Kong, Singapore, Japan, China, Australia, Canada and several European markets. Individual listing/data availability still varies.</p>
            <p>Company search and data requests are cached to reduce repeated calls. Data can be delayed. The public feed does not provide verified bid/ask and session status for actionable day-trading signals.</p>
            <p>Our prototype uses an unofficial connection to Yahoo Finance public responses, rather than a contracted exchange data service. It is not a guaranteed catalogue of every listed company. Before selling the website publicly, use a licensed data provider with the required display/redistribution rights.</p>
            <a class="text-link" asp-page="/Index">Search companies →</a>
        </section>

        }
        @if (!Model.IsPublic) {
        <section class="panel setup-panel"><h2>Import your data</h2><p>Upload daily prices from a permitted source. CSV imports need this exact header and unquoted values:</p><code>date,open,high,low,close,volume</code>
            <p>Dates use YYYY-MM-DD; decimals use a dot. Rows must be ascending and unique. At least 60 completed daily bars are needed for a swing signal; 90 for a backtest.</p>
            <form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" asp-page-handler="Import" class="stack-form">
                <label asp-for="Symbol">Market symbol (CSV only)</label><input asp-for="Symbol" maxlength="30" />
                <label asp-for="CompanyName">Company name (CSV only)</label><input asp-for="CompanyName" maxlength="150" />
                <label class="check"><input asp-for="SplitAdjusted" /> CSV prices are adjusted for stock splits</label>
                <label asp-for="Upload">CSV or dataset JSON (under 3 MB)</label><input asp-for="Upload" type="file" accept=".csv,.json" required />
                <button type="submit">Validate & import</button>
            </form>
            <p>JSON can also include financial metrics. <a class="text-link" href="~/templates/dataset.sample.json" download>Download the fictional JSON template</a>. Keep <code>isSample: true</code> for fictional data. When entering verified real data, replace every sample value and set it to false. Fundamentals need a reporting-period date and a separate <code>valuationAsOf</code> timestamp for the current P/E and EPS. Set <code>isFinancialCompany: true</code> for banks/insurers; the generic model abstains for them.</p>
        </section>
        } else { <section class="panel setup-panel"><h2>Hosted research</h2><p>Search and fetch the enabled provider's company data. File imports are available only in the local personal version. Favourites remain in your browser; public datasets are fetched again after server restarts.</p></section> }
    </div>
</div>
